notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

The two arXiv papers are The Promptware Kill Chain and Invitation Is All You Need. Schneier on Security and Lawfare both cover the promptware kill chain. SafeBreach's post covers the Gemini attack, Embrace The Red's covers ZombAI, and Varonis's covers Reprompt. The last link is a Black Hat webinar.

The background slides name their own sources: the csoh.org glossary and MITRE ATT&CK.

